= Selection bias — Simple =

'''Selection bias''' happens when the people or data included in a study are selected in a way that systematically changes the result.

Imagine asking only people at a gym how often adults exercise. That group may not represent all adults.

Selection bias is not the same as [[Cognitive bias/Simple|cognitive bias]]. Cognitive bias is about patterns in thinking or judgment. Selection bias is about which observations end up in the data.

A huge sample can still be badly biased if it selects the wrong population.

